> g(x: real in 0..1, y: real in 0..1) = exp(x * y)
> integrate g numerically qmc points 1024 replicates 16
∫ exp(x*y) numerically, over the box of its parameters' ranges
  quasi-Monte Carlo (an estimate, not a proof): 1.317852236, standard error 7.5e-05
    16 randomised replicates of 1024 Sobol points in 2 dimensions (Joe-Kuo direction numbers, a random digital shift each; seed 1)
    the error is estimated from the 16 replicates' spread: +-0.00016 at 95% if their means are normal (t = 2.131), which nothing proves
> integrate g numerically qmc points 1024 replicates 16 owen
∫ exp(x*y) numerically, over the box of its parameters' ranges
  quasi-Monte Carlo (an estimate, not a proof): 1.317891724, standard error 7.9e-06
    16 randomised replicates of 1024 Sobol points in 2 dimensions (Joe-Kuo direction numbers, a nested uniform (Owen) scrambling each, from a hash; seed 1)
    the error is estimated from the 16 replicates' spread: +-1.7e-05 at 95% if their means are normal (t = 2.131), which nothing proves
